10 ' DEQQ'S HOUSE II - a real-time 3D adventure for Engine1999, made with the software 3D sector renderer (W3D ...).
20 ' The sequel of the text adventure deqq.bas: Deqq, an alien, crash-landed and lives in an abandoned house. Eight parts of his spaceship are hidden in the house, the
30 ' garden, the shed and the cellar, each behind a small puzzle. Find them (you can carry three things, the big parts and the chair take two places), carry them to the
40 ' wreck at the end of the back yard and build them in. But Deqq is home, and he walks through the house on his round: if he sees you he follows you and carries
50 ' you out of the front door, and what you carried goes back where you found it (the parts already built in stay). Hide in the coat closet, the pantry, behind the
60 ' sofa, in the wardrobe, behind the shower curtain, between the barrels or in the trunk, close doors in his face, run (SHIFT) and listen for his footsteps.
70 ' Nobody is hurt in this game.
80 ' Keys: arrows or WASD walk and turn (A and D slide sideways), SHIFT runs, SPACE jumps, R and F look up and down (HOME looks straight), E or RETURN uses or takes what is
90 ' in front of you (the prompt at the bottom says what), G puts down the last thing you carry, O opens the 3D settings (invert axes, gamma, field of view, turning
100 ' speed; kept for next time), M turns the music on and off, P pauses, Q or ESC quits. Game controller: left stick walks, right stick turns and looks, LT runs, A jumps, X uses and takes, B puts
110 ' down, Y the settings, START pauses, BACK quits. The built parts are saved (the file deqq2.sav of the folder ~/.local/share/<name>/).
120 ' How it is made: the house is DATA (rectangular sectors, walls and portals: demos/levels/deqq2.bas), the pictures are drawn by GFX statements from a table of
130 ' drawing commands (demos/levels/deqq2art.bas) and grabbed into W3D TEXTURE, everything you can touch is a thing (W3D THING) that W3D("DIST"), ("BEARING") and ("SEES")
140 ' find; Deqq walks with W3D THINGMOVE along a route of way points and sees you with W3D("SEES", 0). The whole game logic also runs in the console host without a
150 ' picture, for the test deqq2test.sh: environment DEQQ2_HEADLESS=1 and DEQQ2_PLAY=file (commands; see PLAYBACK).
